       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. Typical doses are 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Overdose toxicity with amlodipine can also be delayed and long-lasting.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose that is sometimes used.\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
